# --- Ad-hoc task queue --------------------------------------------------
# Add these to `crontab -e` on lab01, BELOW the existing CRON_TZ line.
#
# CRON_TZ=America/Chicago MUST already be at the top of the crontab. lab01's
# system timezone is Etc/UTC, so a crontab without it fires 5-6 hours early --
# silently, exiting zero, at the wrong time. Do not remove it.
#
# PATH must also already be set; cron's default environment is too bare to
# find /usr/bin/claude.

# Ad-hoc tasks marked `priority: now` -- every 10 minutes.
# Cheap when the queue is empty: the runner exits immediately without starting
# a Claude session.
*/10 * * * * $HOME/bin/queue-runner.sh --now

# Everything still queued -- once, in the 3-4am window, spaced clear of the
# four existing routines (08 3, 33 3, 56 3 Fri, 17 4 Mondays in August) so two
# full Claude sessions never compete for the same quota.
44 4 * * * $HOME/bin/queue-runner.sh --drain
